        "id": 1124543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-12T23:43:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to protect against the listener blocking the handler thread for an excessive amount of time? Not sure how other platform classes handle this (if at all?).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "de4d58a33a566c2cb2dba20be02d8b08b82ed9d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "246025c4_7adf4a67",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/CarrierPrivilegesTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1463964
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-13T19:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe other platform classes handle this by using one-way Binder calls to ensure that the callback implementations don\u0027t black the handler thread. In this case, a Binder call isn\u0027t necessary at this point because only Telephony entities (which are all in the same process) will be registering listeners.\n\nIf we need to expand this for non-Telephony users in the future, we can reconsider moving to a one-way Binder call. In the meantime, updating the documentation to clarify that long running operations should *not* be done in the #onCarrierPrivilegesChanged method.\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "f365beea_4253a34e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "de4d58a33a566c2cb2dba20be02d8b08b82ed9d3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
